<Application x:Class="Bws.Gui.App"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:ui="http://schemas.lepo.co/wpfui/2022/xaml"
             StartupUri="MainWindow.xaml">

    <!--
        ADR-24. The base of this window's appearance is WPF UI, not the Fluent theme built into
        WPF, and docs/10-WPF-UI.md is required reading before this file changes.

        THERE IS NO ThemeMode HERE AND THERE MUST NOT BE. It is not a leftover. ThemeMode="Dark"
        together with the dictionaries below KILLS THE PROCESS at startup, with
        InvalidOperationException out of ThemeManager.ApplyStyleOnWindow saying
        AllowsTransparency cannot be changed after the window is shown.

        Removing it also fixed something nobody had connected to it: ThemeMode applies a MICA
        backdrop, a window with Mica is translucent to the desktop compositor, and WPF turns
        ClearType OFF on a translucent surface. Measured by counting text pixels carrying
        colour fringing - 0% before, 80.5% after. That was the blurry text.

        Ours are merged LAST on purpose: a dictionary merged later wins, and ours hold the
        values that are ours. Neither of them loads on its own, because both resolve keys that
        arrive with ControlsDictionary.

        THE THEME WAS ONE FILE UNTIL 2026-08-11 AND THE ORDER OF ITS TWO HALVES IS NOT A
        STYLE CHOICE. Controls.xaml reaches the names in Values.xaml through StaticResource,
        which resolves WHILE THE FILE IS BEING READ, so values go before styles and both go
        after the library. Backlog 156. Anywhere else that builds this stack - WpfHost in the
        tests, tools/wpfui-probe - repeats these four lines in this order for the same reason.
    -->
    <Application.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
                <ui:ThemesDictionary Theme="Dark" />
                <ui:ControlsDictionary />
                <ResourceDictionary Source="Themes/Values.xaml" />
                <ResourceDictionary Source="Themes/Controls.xaml" />
            </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </Application.Resources>
</Application>
